/// The queueEntry rows of a set of rooms, for the calls integration: the queue of one media server, which every call on it shares, in one read rather than one per room. A reference field is stored canonical and a bare id compared with it matches nothing, so the ids are made canonical here. actor.userId scoping is not the fix: the calls integration runs as the site owner or the cluster, so a caller term would decide nothing, and what @serverOnly withholds is the WIRE.
@serverOnly
@unbounded("queue entries of the open rooms of one media server -- bounded by the queue entry lifetime and the join rate of the calls policy")
@actor
@cache(0)
query queueEntry callsQueueEntriesForRooms {
  args {
    roomIds  []string!
  }
  filter  row => row.roomId in args.roomIds.select(candidate => canonicalId(candidate, room)) && (row.ownerUserId == actor.userId || actor.isClusterOwner == true)
  shape   callsQueueEntryFull
}

/// One scheduledCall row by its own id. The calls integration reads it before it writes, and to answer a request that names it. actor.userId scoping is not the fix: the calls integration runs as the site owner or the cluster, so a caller term would decide nothing, and what @serverOnly withholds is the WIRE.
@serverOnly
@unbounded("scheduledCall by id -- bounded to a single row (id is the row's own primary key)")
